<div class="three-tool-facts"><div><span>Free tally</span><strong>Optional goals</strong></div><div><span>Presets</span><strong>33/33/34 or 33/33/33</strong></div><div><span>Storage</span><strong>Local browser</strong></div></div>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-meaning"><h3>What is Tasbih and why use a counter?</h3><p>Tasbih commonly describes glorifying Allah, especially through phrases such as SubhanAllah. A digital counter is only an optional memory aid, like fingers or beads; it is not a ritual requirement or a measure of how much worship is accepted. The Quran encourages plentiful remembrance (<a href="https://quran.com/33/41">Quran 33:41</a>). Use a trusted narrated practice when attaching a prescribed count or virtue to a phrase.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-patterns"><h3>33 SubhanAllah, 33 Alhamdulillah and 34 Allahu Akbar</h3><p>One reported form of remembrance after obligatory Salah uses 33 repetitions of SubhanAllah, 33 of Alhamdulillah and 34 of Allahu Akbar, for 100 in total. See <a href="https://sunnah.com/muslim:596a">Sahih Muslim 596a</a> and related narrations. The app gives this its own selectable pattern and moves between each phrase only after the user completes a stage.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-final"><h3>Alternative 33/33/33 plus the Tawhid declaration</h3><p><a href="https://sunnah.com/muslim:597a">Sahih Muslim 597a</a> reports 33 repetitions of each of the three phrases, followed by a final statement of Allah's oneness to complete one hundred. The app shows the last declaration as its own step, with a link to the full exact wording, rather than treating the short phrase 'La ilaha illallah' as a complete quotation of the narration.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-steps"><h3>How to use the online counter step by step</h3><ol><li>Choose free counting or one of the narrated after-Salah presets.</li><li>Tap Count or press Space when focus is outside a form field or button.</li><li>Use Undo for a mistaken tap.</li><li>For a structured preset, finish the displayed target before choosing Next phrase.</li><li>Complete the final stage to record one chosen cycle; do not treat that number as religious merit.</li><li>Use Reset if you want to clear the local count and completed-cycle record.</li></ol></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-example"><h3>Worked example: completing the 33/33/34 pattern</h3><div class="three-tool-example"><p>After selecting <strong>33/33/34</strong>, count SubhanAllah 33 times, then Alhamdulillah 33 times, then Allahu Akbar 34 times. The arithmetic is <strong>33 + 33 + 34 = 100</strong>. The tool asks you to advance between phrases, so reaching 33 once does not automatically claim that all three sections were completed.</p><p>Choosing free counting and a personal goal such as 99 is a different activity: it does not turn that number into an independently authenticated prescription.</p></div></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-technology"><h3>Keyboard access, undo, cycle totals and privacy</h3><p>Spacebar counting excludes inputs, buttons, textareas, editable text and repeated keypresses to avoid accidental tallies. Count, stage and chosen cycles stay in the current browser. An older free-counter value is migrated when there is no current record. Switching between patterns clears the current phrase's count while preserving the recorded number of completed personal cycles.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-differences"><h3>Are Tasbih beads or digital counters required?</h3><p>No particular digital counter is required in order to remember Allah. Scholars discuss preferred counting methods and the use of fingers or beads. A counter may help some people concentrate, but sincerity, correct words and appropriate practice are distinct from the tally. A free target of 100 is not proof of a specified Sunnah for every phrase.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="tasbih-guide-caution"><h3>Avoid mixing source-based dhikr counts</h3><p>Do not add the 33/33/34 and 33/33/33-plus-declaration patterns together as though one newly invented total were prescribed. Do not assume an unverified internet quote promises a reward for every tap. Keep source and setting attached to the chosen dhikr, and consult a qualified teacher about the reported forms.</p></section>
